on"},"8":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-6","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/add-a-project#workflows-that-pick-up-automatically-after-onboarding","content":"Workflows that pick up automatically (after onboarding)"},"9":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-7","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/add-a-project#rules","content":"Rules"},"10":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-8","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project","content":"**Purpose:** one-shot onboarding for a **new project — code repo OR non-code** — into Jackie OS, so everything (registry, vault note, indexes, learnings, sync coverage) is wired *before* real work starts. The agent does all the wiring; for code repos there is **zero** manual setup if the read PAT is scoped to all your repos (see § One-time prerequisite)."},"11":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-9","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project","content":"**Trigger:** \"new project\", \"new code project\", \"new non-code project\", \"register project\", \"I created a repo\", \"set up project X\" — or the agent detects an unregistered project Sergei is starting."},"12":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-10","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project","content":"**Role:** COO + CTO setup."},"13":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-11","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project","content":"**Output:** registry row; `Vault/{Title}.md` note; `Projects.md` / `Home.md` index links; (code) repo bridge + learnings catalog + poller registration; (non-code) `Projects/{Name}/` folder; one commit."},"14":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-12","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#step-0--classify","content":"Ask (or infer): **project name / title**, **type** — `code` (its own git repo) or `non-code` (lives inside jackie-os) — &#x2A;*active?**, and for code: **GitHub remote** (`owner/repo`), **local path**, **default branch** (`main`), &#x2A;*owned or shared?**."},"15":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-13","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#step-0--classify","content":"Then run the matching path. Both end with a single `git commit` in jackie-os."},"16":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-14","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"> **Ownership gate:** if the remote owner isn't Sergei's account (e.g. `AleannLab/…`) or he says it's shared, mark the registry row 🤝 **read-only**, and **skip steps 4–6** (repo bridge, design system, code-repo commit) — Jackie-OS reads a shared repo into the vault but never writes to it and never polls it with the PAT."},"17":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-15","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Registry** — add a `git` row to `System/project-registry.md`: paths, branch, GitHub remote, mirror if any, **Roadmap index** (`plans/roadmap-index.md` — required for owned repos; `—` for shared 🤝)."},"18":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-16","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Vault note + indexes** — `Vault/{Title}.md` (frontmatter `[[Projects]]`, stub, empty `## Status`); add wikilink to `Vault/Projects.md`; if Active, add to `Vault/Home.md` Active list."},"19":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-17","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Learnings** — `Vault/Agent-Learnings/{Title} learnings.md` from the Newfin learnings template; add a row to `Vault/Agent-Learnings/Index.md`."},"20":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-18","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Repo bridge** (in the **code repo** — owned only): copy `System/templates/JACKIE-OS-bridge.md` → `docs/JACKIE-OS.md` (fill KEY, vault note, branch); scaffold `docs/solutions/README.md` if missing; add the **Vault sync** paragraph to the repo's `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` (point to `docs/JACKIE-OS.md`)."},"21":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-19","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Plans scaffold** (owned code repos only — skip 🤝 shared):"},"22":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-20","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"Create `plans/` from `System/templates/plans/`: `README.md`, `roadmap-index.md`, `future-improvements.md`, `archive/README.md`."},"23":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-21","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"Replace placeholders: `{PROJECT}` = display name, `{DATE}` = today `YYYY-MM-DD`, `{INITIAL_SHA}` = `git rev-parse --short HEAD` (or `0000000` before first commit)."},"24":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-22","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"Append planning section to `CLAUDE.md` (create `## Planning` if missing). Mirror one line in `AGENTS.md` if present."},"25":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-23","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"In vault note `## Status` stub, link `plans/roadmap-index.md` as the forward-work surface."},"26":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-24","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Do not** copy Newfin/Rodyna-specific archives — empty `plans/archive/` except README."},"27":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-25","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Design system** (owned code repos — skip API-only / CLI-only / shared 🤝):"},"28":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-26","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**When:** Step 0 expects a user-facing UI, *or* the repo already has a frontend package (`web/`, `miniapp/`, `frontend/`, `apps/*/web`, or a subdir with `react`/`vue`/`svelte` in `package.json`). If Sergei says \"no UI\", skip."},"29":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-27","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Doc path** (first match):"},"30":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-28","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"`miniapp/` → `miniapp/docs/design-memory.md`"},"31":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-29","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"`web/` at repo root → `docs/design-system.md` (token source: `web/src/styles/globals.css` or project's token file)"},"32":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-30","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"other UI package `{pkg}/` → `{pkg}/docs/design-memory.md`"},"33":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-31","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"UI planned but not scaffolded yet → `docs/design-system.md` at repo root (`{UI_PACKAGE}` = *TBD*, `{TOKEN_SOURCE}` = *TBD*)"},"34":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-32","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"Copy design system template; replace `{PROJECT}`, `{UI_PACKAGE}`, `{TOKEN_SOURCE}`. Template includes YAML frontmatter (DESIGN.md format) + prose; fill anchor token values from the token CSS file. Do not overwrite an existing design doc — merge or skip if one is already canonical (e.g. Newfin `docs/design-system.md`, Rodyna `miniapp/docs/design-memory.md`)."},"35":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-33","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"Add &#x2A;*`design:lint`** to the repo root `package.json` (or UI workspace `package.json` if no root scripts): `\"design:lint\": \"npx -p @google/design.md@0.3.0 designmd lint &#60;DESIGN_DOC_REL>\"` — path matches the doc from the bullet above."},"36":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-34","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"Append the **UI** section from design section template to `AGENTS.md` and/or `CLAUDE.md` (replace `{UI_PACKAGE}`, `{DESIGN_DOC_REL}`). Skip if an equivalent section already points at the design doc."},"37":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-35","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Page-load benchmark (FF 003):** copy benchmark page-load template into the repo (path per layout — e.g. `docs/performance.md` or `{UI_PACKAGE}/docs/performance.md`). Scaffold benchmark script from Newfin (`server/src/scripts/benchmark-page-load.ts`) or Rodyna (`miniapp/scripts/benchmark-page-load.ts`) pattern. Add `npm run benchmark:pages` + Definition of done line: *new screen → add to benchmark; all routes \\<50ms p50 warm*."},"38":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-36","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"Optional later (not required at onboarding): `npm run setup:ui` + mock API + deep links — see Rodyna `miniapp/README.md` § Plain-browser design work."},"39":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-37","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Commit in the code repo** — bridge + solutions + &#x2A;*plans/** + design doc + AGENTS/CLAUDE blurbs in one PR or push."},"40":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-38","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Poller — nothing to do.** The merge-poll is **registry-driven** (`.github/scripts/merge_poll.py` reads `project-registry.md`), so adding the row in **A1** already puts the repo under the intraday poll (owned `sc-jackie/*`, Active, not shared)."},"41":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-39","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Project-sync** — run project-sync; prepend the vault `## Status` stub; refresh `hot.md` if Active."},"42":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-40","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-a--code-project-own-git-repo","content":"**Linear** (owned repos) — add the project to Linear. Hermes can then delegate bounded work to temporary Cursor ACP workers when needed."},"43":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-41","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-b--non-code-project-lives-inside-jackie-os","content":"No GitHub repo, no bridge, no Action, no secret — the work is *in* the vault, so the commit **is** the sync."},"44":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-42","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-b--non-code-project-lives-inside-jackie-os","content":"**Folder** — create `Projects/{Name}/` for working files; add `Projects/{Name}/STATUS.md` only if you want a `status-file` mirror."},"45":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-43","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-b--non-code-project-lives-inside-jackie-os","content":"**Plans scaffold** — create `Projects/{Name}/plans/` from project plans templates: `README.md`, `roadmap-index.md`, `future-improvements.md`, `archive/README.md`. Replace `{PROJECT}`, `{VAULT_NOTE}`, `{DATE}`. Registry **Roadmap index** → `Projects/{Name}/plans/roadmap-index.md`."},"46":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-44","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-b--non-code-project-lives-inside-jackie-os","content":"**Registry** — add a `vault` row (or `status-file` row if you made a STATUS.md) to `System/project-registry.md` with Roadmap index path from step 2."},"47":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-45","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-b--non-code-project-lives-inside-jackie-os","content":"**Vault note + indexes** — `Vault/{Title}.md` (frontmatter, stub, empty `## Status`); wikilink in `Vault/Projects.md`; Active list in `Home.md` if active. Link `Projects/{Name}/plans/roadmap-index.md` in the stub."},"48":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-46","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#path-b--non-code-project-lives-inside-jackie-os","content":"**Commit** — `git commit` jackie-os. Done — morning-brief + wrap-up track it from here."},"49":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-47","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#one-time-prerequisite-sergei-once-ever--not-per-project","content":"For code repos to get **intraday** merge-poll coverage, jackie-os needs one secret:"},"50":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-48","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#one-time-prerequisite-sergei-once-ever--not-per-project","content":"Create **one** fine-grained PAT → **Contents: Read**, scoped to **All repositories** under `sc-jackie` (so every future repo is auto-covered — no per-project secret work)."},"51":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-49","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#one-time-prerequisite-sergei-once-ever--not-per-project","content":"Add it to jackie-os → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → &#x2A;*`JACKIE_OS_READ_PAT`**."},"52":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-50","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#one-time-prerequisite-sergei-once-ever--not-per-project","content":"Skip this and code repos still sync **daily** via the 07:30 morning-brief — you just lose the intraday entry. Non-code projects need nothing."},"53":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-51","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#verification","content":"`project-sync` shows the new row without errors (path exists, or flagged skip)."},"54":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-52","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#verification","content":"Vault note + index links exist; (code) learnings catalog + `Index.md` row present."},"55":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-53","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#verification","content":"**Code, owned:** `docs/JACKIE-OS.md` + `docs/solutions/README.md&#x60; + &#x2A;*`plans/`** (roadmap-index, future-improvements, README, archive/) committed in the repo; `CLAUDE.md` **Planning** section; repo in merge poll via registry. &#x2A;*UI repos:** design doc + `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` UI section + **page-load benchmark** (`npm run benchmark:pages`, \\<50ms p50 DoD) — or documented skip reason. &#x2A;*Shared (🤝):** confirm NOTHING was written/pushed to the repo, Roadmap index = `—`, and it's NOT in `merge_poll.py`."},"56":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-54","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#verification","content":"**Non-code:** `Projects/{Name}/&#x60; + &#x2A;*`Projects/{Name}/plans/`** + vault note committed; no repo/bridge/Action created."},"57":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-55","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#workflows-that-pick-up-automatically-after-onboarding","content":"Workflow"},"58":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-56","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#workflows-that-pick-up-automatically-after-onboarding","content":"How it finds the project"},"59":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-57","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#workflows-that-pick-up-automatically-after-onboarding","content":"**project-sync**"},"60":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-58","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#workflows-that-pick-up-automatically-after-onboarding","content":"`System/project-registry.md`"},"61":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-59","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#workflows-that-pick-up-automatically-after-onboarding","content":"**morning-brief (07:30)**"},"62":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-60","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#workflows-that-pick-up-automatically-after-onboarding","content":"Active registry rows → rich vault Status daily (authoritative sync)"},"63":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-61","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#workflows-that-pick-up-automatically-after-onboarding","content":"**merge-poll (\\~3h)**"},"64":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-62","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#workflows-that-pick-up-automatically-after-onboarding","content":"`.github/scripts/merge_poll.py` REPOS — code repos only, thin intraday entry"},"65":{"id":"/docs/add-a-project-63","page_id":"/docs/add-a-project","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/add-a-project#workflows-that-pick-up-automatically-after-onboarding","content