l":"/docs/architecture#rules-that-keep-the-system-simple","content":"Keep active project state in Linear."},"121":{"id":"/docs/architecture-40","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rules-that-keep-the-system-simple","content":"Use Hermes for the always-on loop."},"122":{"id":"/docs/architecture-41","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rules-that-keep-the-system-simple","content":"Create temporary workers only when a bounded task needs them."},"123":{"id":"/docs/architecture-42","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#rules-that-keep-the-system-simple","content":"Sync shipped state back into the vault."},"124":{"id":"/docs/catalog","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"page","content":"System Catalog","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Look it up"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog"},"125":{"id":"/docs/catalog-0","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog","content":"Every skill and script in Jackie-OS — the map to navigate the system."},"126":{"id":"/docs/catalog-1","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"Skills vs Scripts — decision"},"127":{"id":"/docs/catalog-2","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"How it fits together (30-second orientation)"},"128":{"id":"/docs/catalog-3","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#skills--grouped-by-job","content":"Skills — grouped by job"},"129":{"id":"/docs/catalog-4","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#what-runs-when-cron","content":"What runs when (cron)"},"130":{"id":"/docs/catalog-5","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog","content":"> **The map.** Every skill (what the AI does) and script (what runs on a schedule or on demand). Start here to navigate the system. Depth links: skills → Skills Registry; what-runs-when → Hermes VPS crontab + Vault Rhythm; operating → Cheat Sheet."},"131":{"id":"/docs/catalog-6","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"**Skills** are LLM judgment playbooks — markdown decision trees that agents follow when running a task (example: `morning-brief.md` = what a brief contains, how to read vault/email, when to alert, how to publish). Skills are the AI's **thinking layer**; they live in `System/skills/` and the agent reads them whole, then improvises per context."},"132":{"id":"/docs/catalog-7","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"**Scripts** are the mechanics layer — bash or Python executables that handle scheduling, filesystem operations, subprocess calls, and state management (example: `morning-brief-vps.py` = pull vault, run the skill in the Hermes sandbox, format output, write to file, deliver). Scripts live in `System/{coo,capture,ops,periodic,work,lib,scripts}/` and are the **source of truth** — edits go here, never the VPS copy (symlinked)."},"133":{"id":"/docs/catalog-8","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"**Pattern:** Skills call scripts (or describe the sequence scripts follow). A typical cron job is a thin `&#60;name>.sh` wrapper (cron entry) that execs a `&#60;name>.py` (logic). When the LLM is involved, it's one `hermes -z` call returning text that the script writes."},"134":{"id":"/docs/catalog-9","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Skills** = markdown playbooks the AI (Claude/Hermes) follows. Some are agent-run (judgment), some are implemented mechanically by a script."},"135":{"id":"/docs/catalog-10","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Scripts** = the executable layer. They live in the repo under `System/{coo,capture,ops,periodic,work,lib,scripts}/` and are the **source of truth**. On the VPS they're symlinked into `~/.hermes/scripts/` by `hermes-vps-link-scripts.sh` (rebuilt on every autodeploy `git pull`). &#x2A;*Edit the repo copy, never the VPS copy.**"},"136":{"id":"/docs/catalog-11","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Two schedulers:** the **Hermes agent-cron** (`~/.hermes/cron/jobs.json`, edited via the dashboard — the morning stack) and the **OS crontab** (`hermes-vps-crontab.txt` — deploy/health/weekly)."},"137":{"id":"/docs/catalog-12","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Pattern:** most cron jobs are a thin `&#60;name>.sh` wrapper (cron entry) that execs a `&#60;name>.py` (the logic). `no_agent` jobs are mechanical; the LLM, when used, is one `hermes -z` call returning text that the Python writes."},"138":{"id":"/docs/catalog-13","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills--grouped-by-job","content":"Full registry: Skills Registry."},"139":{"id":"/docs/catalog-14","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills--grouped-by-job","content":"Skill"},"140":{"id":"/docs/catalog-15","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills--grouped-by-job","content":"Does"},"141":{"id":"/docs/catalog-16","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills--grouped-by-job","content":"Implemented by"},"142":{"id":"/docs/catalog-17","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills--grouped-by-job","content":"**Capture**"},"143":{"id":"/docs/catalog-18","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type