"/docs/concepts#okf-open-knowledge-format-bundle","content":"OKF (Open Knowledge Format) bundle"},"340":{"id":"/docs/concepts-7","page_id":"/docs/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-agent","content":"Hermes Agent"},"341":{"id":"/docs/concepts-8","page_id":"/docs/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts#two-bot-model","content":"Two-bot model"},"342":{"id":"/docs/concepts-9","page_id":"/docs/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts#operating-model","content":"Operating model"},"343":{"id":"/docs/concepts-10","page_id":"/docs/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts#sync-modes--vault-writeback","content":"Sync modes — vault writeback"},"344":{"id":"/docs/concepts-11","page_id":"/docs/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts#telegram-boundary","content":"Telegram boundary"},"345":{"id":"/docs/concepts-12","page_id":"/docs/concepts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts#what-lives-where-post-2026-06-29-restructure","content":"What lives where (post-2026-06-29 restructure)"},"346":{"id":"/docs/concepts-13","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts","content":"> Shared domain vocabulary for this project — entities, named processes, and status concepts with project-specific meaning. Seeded with core domain vocabulary, then accretes as learnings; direct edits are fine. Glossary only, not a spec or catch-all."},"347":{"id":"/docs/concepts-14","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**hot.md** — A \\~500-word cache in `Vault/hot.md` of current focus and open loops, refreshed at every session end; fastest orientation for any agent starting a new session."},"348":{"id":"/docs/concepts-15","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**wrap-up** — The wrap-up skill that syncs the vault, updates `## Status` in project notes, refreshes `hot.md`, and commits."},"349":{"id":"/docs/concepts-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**brief** — An AI-generated daily or period summary (morning brief, weekly brief) that reads code activity, vault status, and calendar to inform the day."},"350":{"id":"/docs/concepts-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**skill** — A repeatable workflow playbook (markdown + optional code) living in `System/skills/`; an AI reads it and executes the defined steps. Global owned skills carry the `jos-` prefix (see Skills Registry)."},"351":{"id":"/docs/concepts-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**Hermes Agent** — The Nous Research agent that runs the always-on COO loop: briefs, capture, knowledge work, ops, scheduling, and orchestration."},"352":{"id":"/docs/concepts-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**Persik** — Two Telegram bots: `@Persik_finbot` (the Newfin-hosted product bot) and `@persik_hermes_bot` (the full Hermes VPS channel)."},"353":{"id":"/docs/concepts-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**workers** — Temporary Cursor ACP workers used for bounded code, design, or research tasks. The old named Buzz/Cyrus fleet was retired on 2026-08-07."},"354":{"id":"/docs/concepts-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**registry** — The `System/project-registry.md` file that maps each project to its code repo and/or STATUS file, serving as the single source of truth for sync."},"355":{"id":"/docs/concepts-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#occasional","content":"**janitor** — An OKF linter and maintenance tool that audits frontmatter compliance and keeps the vault structure clean (quarterly cron)."},"356":{"id":"/docs/concepts-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#occasional","content":"**docs-first** — Before building anything new, check the master index for prior art; on ship, update the owning doc in the same commit."},"357":{"id":"/docs/concepts-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#deprecated--winding-down","content":"**Cowork** — The Claude desktop app's scheduled-tasks harness on Sergei's Mac. **Effectively retired** — a single leftover schedule remains (Sunday 18:00 weekly-review); everything else runs on the VPS."},"358":{"id":"/docs/concepts-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#deprecated--winding-down","content":"**Bases/Ops board** — Retired Obsidian task board. Active project tracking now lives in Linear."},"359":{"id":"/docs/concepts-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#jackie-os-agent-any-editor-hermes-optional","content":"Jackie OS is portable files — the vault, the skills, the rules. Any AI coding tool that opens the `~/Jackie-OS` folder (**Claude Code**, **Cursor**, **Codex**) auto-reads `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` and runs the skills that live inside it, *becoming* a Jackie OS agent; the skills aren't moved or copied — a few cross-project ones (e.g. `wrap up`) are installed once in `~/.agents/skills/`. `wrap up` from any editor syncs the vault, `## Status`, and `hot.md`, then commits. **Hermes** (below) is simply the always-on instance of that same agent on the VPS — it runs the schedule unattended. Hermes is not required to use the system; it only automates the loop."},"360":{"id":"/docs/concepts-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#okf-open-knowledge-format-bundle","content":"Jackie-OS adopts **Open Knowledge Format** *frontmatter* — every skill, solution, concept, project note, daily, and brief carries structured YAML (`type`, `title`, `timestamp`, …). This makes the vault a **portable, vendor-neutral knowledge bundle**: anyone can fork the structure and wire a different automation layer, and any agent can orient and retrieve by metadata instead of inferring from prose. **Frontmatter only** — internal links stay as Obsidian wikilinks (OKF's relative-link convention is *not* adopted). Backfilled by `System/tools/add-okf-frontmatter.py`; enforced by `janitor` OKF lint mode. Headline goal = portability; faster agent orientation/retrieval is the day-to-day payoff."},"361":{"id":"/docs/concepts-28","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#hermes-agent","content":"Hermes Agent runs on the VPS as the always-on COO and orchestrator. The provider and model can change without changing Jackie-OS: the durable layer is the vault, the skills, and the operating rules."},"362":{"id":"/docs/concepts-29","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#two-bot-model","content":"Two live Telegram bots, split by audience:"},"363":{"id":"/docs/concepts-30","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#two-bot-model","content":"**@Persik\\_finbot** — the Newfin finance product bot."},"364":{"id":"/docs/concepts-31","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#two-bot-model","content":"**@persik\\_hermes\\_bot** — the Jackie-OS COO surface for briefs, capture, knowledge work, and operations."},"365":{"id":"/docs/concepts-32","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#operating-model","content":"**bb** is the primary interactive desk."},"366":{"id":"/docs/concepts-33","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#operating-model","content":"**Hermes Agent** owns the always-on COO loop and orchestration."},"367":{"id":"/docs/concepts-34","p