inear)** — team `EVE`, workspace `evegelin`. `bunit` + `b-unit` share the **B-Unit** product project (backlog + agent loop, `Pipeline` = `dev`/`content`/`research`); the TikTok/marketing production pipeline lives in a separate **B-Unit — Content** project (episode-per-issue, milestones = weeks). Labels are one workspace-wide 3-group taxonomy — `Pipeline` · `Stage` (needs-refinement/needs-approval) · `Type` (Bug/Feature/Improvement) — shared by every project, nothing to recreate per repo. The active code portfolio, including **Draw**, is tracked in Linear. Non-code projects remain in Bases."},"906":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-115","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"**Tracker switch (`tracker: linear | bases`)** — the per-project flag that project-sync and morning-brief branch on. Default is `bases` for **every** row (task state from `git`/`status-file` + the Obsidian Ops Bases, exactly as before — no change). A row flips to `linear` once its Linear board exists: its task/plan state is then read from Linear via `System/scripts/linear-fetch.py` (`--project &#60;Linear project name>`) **instead of** the Ops Bases, closing the \"Linear-only work invisible until /wrap-up\" gap (esp. `content`/`research` issues with no PR). Migrate one row at a time; flip back to `bases` to revert."},"907":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-116","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"**`tracker: linear`** → `jackie-os` → Jackie OS project; `b-unit`, `bunit` → B-Unit; `rodyna` → Rodyna; `newfin` → Newfin; `sergeichan` → Personal Website; `draw` → Draw (agent-team enabled; routing label `Draw`)."},"908":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-117","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"**`tracker: bases`** → every other active row (default; unchanged behavior)."},"909":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-118","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"**Source types**"},"910":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-119","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"Source"},"911":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-120","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"Truth"},"912":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-121","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"Sync direction"},"913":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-122","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"`git`"},"914":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-123","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"`origin/&#60;branch>` + local clone health"},"915":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-124","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"repo → vault `## Status`; optional mirror → `STATUS.md`"},"916":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-125","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"`status-file`"},"917":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-126","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"`Projects/*/STATUS.md`"},"918":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-127","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"STATUS → vault `## Status`; vault one-liner → mirror footer"},"919":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-128","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"`vault`"},"920":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-129","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"vault note file in Jackie-OS git"},"921":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-130","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"jackie-os git log on that file → vault `## Status` (dormant projects)"},"922":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-131","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"A `git` row whose **GitHub** cell carries 🤝 (or whose Source shows `⚠️ shared`) is a repo Sergei **does not own** — e.g. `AleannLab/draw`, co-owned with a collaborator. For these repos:"},"923":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-132","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Default is READ-ONLY.** project-sync may diff `origin/&#60;branch>` → update the vault `## Status` and `STATUS.md` mirror. It must not push, commit, branch, or open a PR on a shared repo unless Sergei explicitly authorizes that repository."},"924":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-133","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Draw exception (authorized 2026-07-12):** `AleannLab/draw` is an active Linear agent-team code project. A delegated agent may implement an issue in an isolated worktree and open a normal reviewable PR; do not push directly to `main`. This exception applies only to Draw, not other shared rows."},"925":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-134","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**No Jackie-OS scaffolding.** Never add `docs/JACKIE-OS.md`, `docs/solutions/`, an Agent-Learnings `## Jackie-OS sync` paragraph in the repo's `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md`, or any other Jackie-OS bookkeeping file. Bridge/learnings/compound write-ups stay on the Jackie-OS side only (vault note + `Vault/Agent-Learnings/{Title} learnings.md`). Skipped because: any PR there lands in the collaborator's repo."},"926":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-135","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Merge-poll:** owned repos are covered by the central Action in jackie-os (registry-driven). No per-repo sync tokens or Cursor automations."},"927":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-136","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"Only **actual app changes** Sergei makes himself belong in a shared repo — never agent housekeeping."},"928":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-137","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Add a row** when a project gets a vault note — never hardcode paths in skills. &#x2A;*New project (code or non-code):** run skill Add a Project (registry + vault + **plans scaffold** + bridge + learnings + poller registration)."},"929":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-138","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Plans surface (owned code repos):** every new owned repo gets `plans/roadmap-index.md` + `plans/future-improvements.md` at onboarding. Non-code projects get `Projects/{Name}/plans/`. After each ship: wrap-up § Catalog cleanup."},"930":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-139","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Code-repo bridge:** each **owned** `git` row should have `docs/JACKIE-OS.md` in the repo (template: `System/templates/JACKIE-OS-bridge.md`) so Cursor/Claude Code sessions know to run project-sync from Jackie-OS at session end. **Shared repos (🤝) get NO bridge** — see Write policy above."},"931":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-140","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Use these when writing skills, bridge docs, or Agent-Learnings catalogs. Registry **Path** column uses the Mac home form; agents on other machines substitute."},"932":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-141","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Context"},"933":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-142","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Jackie-OS root"},"934":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-143","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Example code repo"},"935":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-144","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"**Mac (Sergei)**"},"936":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-145","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"`~/Jackie-OS/`"},"937":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-146","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"`~/dev/newfin/`"},"938":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-147","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"**Linux / Cursor cloud**"},"939":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-148","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"`/workspace/` (or clone path)"},"940":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-149","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Must exist locally for `git` rows — see cloud note below"},"941":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-150","page_