e_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"The tools, in plain words"},"1418":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-12","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-core-idea-in-one-line","content":"The core idea in one line"},"1419":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-13","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-is","content":"A **second brain** and an **always-on AI COO**, wired so the agent knows what is in the brain."},"1420":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-14","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-is","content":"The second brain is your Obsidian vault: every journal entry, project note, decision, and idea, linked and versioned in git. It compounds over time. Hermes Agent by Nous Research runs the daily loop and delivers results back to Telegram."},"1421":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-15","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-is","content":"You think and decide. The brain remembers. The agent acts."},"1422":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-16","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"Every time you open ChatGPT or Claude, it starts with zero context. You re-explain your projects, your priorities, what you shipped last week. The AI helps inside a session. Across sessions it forgets."},"1423":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-17","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"Most people also keep this split:"},"1424":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-18","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"Notes (diary, ideas, plans) in one app"},"1425":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-19","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"Code projects in separate folders"},"1426":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-20","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"AI in a chat window that forgot everything"},"1427":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-21","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-problem-this-solves","content":"Nothing shares memory. Jackie OS makes all three read from the same source."},"1428":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-22","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"The vault is a folder of markdown files you open in Obsidian. Notes link to each other like Wikipedia: `[[Newfin]]`, `[[Warsaw]]`, `[[2026-06-20]]`. Over time you get a web: journal connects to projects, projects connect to decisions, decisions connect to people."},"1429":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-23","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"What lives there:"},"1430":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-24","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Written by you"},"1431":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-25","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Written by the agent"},"1432":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-26","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Daily journal"},"1433":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-27","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Morning brief + weekly / monthly / yearly reviews"},"1434":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-28","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Project ideas, decisions"},"1435":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-29","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Project `## Status` (synced from code)"},"1436":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-30","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Notes on people, places"},"1437":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-31","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Clippings (links you sent) + person profiles"},"1438":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-32","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Beliefs, theses"},"1439":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-33","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Coaching notes, link suggestions, `hot.md` cache"},"1440":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-34","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"**hot.md** is the key mechanism: after every sync, the agent writes a fresh \\~500-word summary of what's currently active. Every AI session (Cursor, Claude Code, Hermes) reads this first. Context holds because there's a standing summary of where you are."},"1441":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-35","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"The vault is git-versioned. Nothing gets lost. The agent never edits your journal entries. It only appends to the end, or writes into its own files."},"1442":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-36","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-second-brain-vault","content":"Every file also carries a little structured metadata (`type`, `title`, `date`) in a format called **OKF** (Open Knowledge Format). You never see it, but it makes the vault *portable*: not locked to any one tool: and lets any agent orient and retrieve by metadata instead of guessing from prose."},"1443":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-37","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"The system isn't one feature. It's a set of jobs the agent does for you, all reading from and writing to the same second brain."},"1444":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-38","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Vaulting & linking** means keeping one git-versioned source of truth *and* weaving it into a graph. Every note, brief, and decision lives in the vault; nothing is scattered or lost. After each brief, the agent also suggests links between notes you wrote: \"this journal entry relates to \\[\\[Newfin]], to \\[\\[Warsaw]]\": so over time the vault becomes a connected web, not a pile of files."},"1445":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-39","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Capturing** means pulling stuff *into* the brain without friction. DM the Telegram bot a thought → it lands in today's journal within the hour. Send a link → it gets filed into Clippings. Type `meet Sarah:` with notes → it creates a meeting entry *and* a person note for Sarah."},"1446":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-40","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Briefing** means telling you where you are. Morning brief (daily), weekly review (Sunday), monthly and yearly reviews. Each reads the vault + your code and summarizes what changed, what's next, what's blocked."},"1447":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-41","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Syncing** means keeping code and notes in agreement. The agent reads git history from your repos and writes it into each project's `## Status` note, so the vault always reflects what actually shipped."},"1448":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-42","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Building** stays deliberate. Sergei works in bb and can delegate bounded code, design, or research tasks to temporary Cursor ACP workers. Linear keeps the project record, and shipped work syncs back into the vault."},"1449":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-43","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Researching** means digging on demand. Say `research &lt;topic>` and it sweeps Reddit, HN, X, markets (last 30 days) and files the findings into the vault."},"1450":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-44","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Coaching** is the reflective layer. Recovery, identity, and \"fractal\" period reviews: week, month, year: where the agent takes a coach stance and walks you through patterns instead of just reporting facts."},"1451":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-45","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"**Enriching** means filling in context. New person shows up in your notes? The agent pulls a public profile and adds a `## Public profile` section to their note."},"1452":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-46","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-it-actually-does","content":"Each of these is a **skill**: a markdown playbook the agent follows. They all share the same vault, so capturing feeds briefing, briefing feeds coaching, and nothing has to be re-explained between them."},"1453":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-47","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"The jobs above are *what* it does. Hermes Agent by Nous Research is *who* runs the always-on loop. It works on a schedule while you sleep, and you can reach it by DMing `@persik_hermes_bot` on Telegram. It handles briefs, sync, research, journal capture, knowledge work, ops, and orchestration."},"1454":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-48","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"Three things make it an agent rather than a script:"},"1455":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-49","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"**It runs itself.** A schedule on the server fires the jobs: morning brief at 07:30, journal capture hourly, weekly review Sunday. Your Mac can be off and traveling; the loop still runs."},"1456":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-50","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"**It follows playbooks, not hardcode.** Each job is a **skill**: a markdown file in `System/skills/` that lives *in the vault*. You read and edit them like any other note. Change the playbook, change the behavior."},"1457":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-51","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"**It's not a black box.** Everything it reads comes from the vault; everything it writes goes back to the vault. The full chain is auditable: no hidden state."},"1458":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-52","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-agent-hermes","content":"There's a second, separate bot: `@Persik_finbot`: that handles money and finance for the Newfin app. Hermes (`@persik_hermes_bot`) is the one that runs your OS."},"1459":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-53","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#hermes-is-optional-it-lives-in-a-folder","content":"Hermes is the *always-on* layer: it runs the schedule on a server while you sleep. But you don't need it to use Jackie OS."},"1460":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-54","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#hermes-is-optional-it-lives-in-a-folder","content":"At its core, Jackie OS is just a folder of files: your notes, skills, and rules. bb is the primary interactive desk, but any capable tool can read the same folder and use the same memory."},"1461":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-55","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#hermes-is-optional-it-lives-in-a-folder","content":"Nothing \"migrates\": you just connect the folder. Say **wrap up** from any of these tools and the vault syncs, project `## Status` blocks update, `hot.md` refreshes, and the changes commit: exactly the loop Hermes runs, just triggered by hand."},"1462":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-56","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#hermes-is-optional-it-lives-in-a-folder","content":"So: &#x2A;*Hermes runs the always-on loop. bb is the hands-on desk. The folder is the shared brain.**"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-57","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-they-connect","content":"It's a loop, not a pipeline. You feed the vault (journaling, DMs, code). Hermes reads the vault + git, does its jobs, writes back to the vault, and pings you on Telegram. Your DMs flow back into the vault. Round and round."},"1464":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-58","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-they-connect","content":"The glue is **hot.md**. When *any* Claude session starts: terminal, Cursor, Hermes: it reads hot.md first and walks in knowing your current focus, last merge, what's pending. That's the trick that kills the cold start."},"1465":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-59","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-they-connect","content":"For the system diagram, see the docs site \"The system map\" page."},"1466":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-60","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"**07:30*&#x2A;: Hermes wakes up (you're asleep), reads all your code repos, sees what merged, syncs project status notes, writes the brief, sends it to your Telegram. Done before you check your phone. &#x2A;(Research is on-demand now: say `research &lt;topic>` whenever you want it; it no longer runs unattended at 06:45.)*"},"1467":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-61","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"**Morning**: You read the brief over coffee. Reply to Hermes via Telegram DM if you want to add something to your journal. It captures it within the hour."},"1468":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-62","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"**Day**: You work, code, journal in Obsidian. When you finish a planning session or push code, say **wrap up**: Hermes syncs the vault immediately."},"1469":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-63","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"**Sunday 18:00**: Weekly review runs automatically. Patterns, what compounded, what to carry forward."},"1470":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-64","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#how-a-day-actually-feels","content":"**Nothing requires you.** The morning stack runs on the VPS even when your Mac is off and you're traveling."},"1471":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-65","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"**Yes:**"},"1472":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-66","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Write briefs and reviews into `Vault/Briefs/`"},"1473":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-67","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Update `## Status` blocks in project notes"},"1474":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-68","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Append to today's journal (Telegram capture only: end of file)"},"1475":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-69","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Refresh `hot.md` after every sync"},"1476":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-70","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"**Never:**"},"1477":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-71","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Edit the body of your journal entries"},"1478":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-72","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Touch notes tagged `private`"},"1479":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-73","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Rename vault notes (that breaks Obsidian links: human-only)"},"1480":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-74","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#what-the-agent-is-allowed-to-touch","content":"Put credentials in any markdown file"},"1481":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-75","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"The schedule covers the daily loop. These are the things you trigger by hand:"},"1482":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-76","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"Say"},"1483":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-77","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"What it does"},"1484":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-78","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"**wrap up**"},"1485":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-79","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"After vault work or a code push: syncs everything now instead of waiting for 07:30"},"1486":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-80","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"**sync projects**"},"1487":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-81","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"Quick mid-session \"where are we?\" status check"},"1488":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-82","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"**research \\<topic>**"},"1489":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-83","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"Deep community/market dig (Reddit, HN, X, markets) filed into the vault"},"1490":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-84","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"**morning brief**"},"1491":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-85","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"Trigger the brief now instead of waiting"},"1492":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-86","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"**coach me**"},"1493":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-87","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"Reflective session: recovery, identity, patterns"},"1494":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-88","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"**weekly / monthly / yearly review**"},"1495":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-89","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"Run a period review on demand instead of waiting for its schedule"},"1496":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-90","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-commands-everything-else-is-automatic","content":"The morning stack, hourly journal capture, and Sunday review all run on their own: you never trigger those."},"1497":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-91","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"None of these need to be understood to use the system: but here's what each one is, in one line:"},"1498":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-92","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"Tool"},"1499":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-93","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"What it is"},"1500":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-94","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"**Obsidian**"},"1501":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-95","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"A free notes app. Your vault is just a folder of plain text files it opens."},"1502":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-96","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"**Markdown**"},"1503":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-97","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"Plain text with simple formatting (like `**bold**`). Future-proof: opens anywhere, forever."},"1504":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-98","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"**Git**"},"1505":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-99","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"A time machine for files. Every change is saved and reversible; nothing is ever truly lost."},"1506":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-100","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"**VPS**"},"1507":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-101","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"A small computer rented in a data center that never sleeps: so the agent runs even when your laptop is closed."},"1508":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-102","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"**AI provider**"},"1509":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-103","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"A swappable model or coding tool. The vault and skills do not depend on one provider."},"1510":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-104","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"**Hermes Agent**"},"1511":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-105","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"The Nous Research agent that runs the always-on COO loop and orchestration."},"1512":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-106","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"**Telegram**"},"1513":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-107","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"The messaging app you use to talk to the agent (the bot is called Persik)."},"1514":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-108","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"**Skill**"},"1515":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-109","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"A markdown file of instructions telling the agent how to do one job. Editable like any note."},"1516":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-110","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"**OKF**"},"1517":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-111","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-tools-in-plain-words","content":"Open Knowledge Format: structured metadata (`type`, `title`, `date`) on every file. Makes the vault a portable, vendor-neutral bundle any agent can orient in and retrieve from: not locked to one tool."},"1518":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-112","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-core-idea-in-one-line","content":"**Your thinking goes into the vault. The agent reads it, acts on it, and keeps it current. You never start from zero.**"},"1519":{"id":"/docs/what-it-does-113","page_id":"/docs/what-it-does","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/what-it-does#the-core-idea-in-one-line","content":"*Updated 2026-08-14: bb desk, Hermes Agent COO loop, temporary ACP workers, and Linear tracking.*"},"1520":{"id":"/docs/workers","page_id":"/docs/workers","type":"page","content":"Current flow","breadcrumbs":["Docs","What runs by itself?"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/workers"},"1521":{"id":"/docs/workers-0","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers","content":"How bb, Hermes, temporary workers, and Linear fit together."},"1522":{"id":"/docs/workers-1","page_id":"/docs/workers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workers#current-flow","content":"Current flow"},"1523":{"id":"/docs/workers-2","page_id":"/docs/workers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workers#interaction-flow","content":"Interaction flow"},"1524":{"id":"/docs/workers-3","page_id":"/docs/workers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workers#telegram-surfaces","content":"Telegram surfaces"},"1525":{"id":"/docs/workers-4","page_id":"/docs/workers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/workers#retired-fleet","content":"Retired fleet"},"1526":{"id":"/docs/workers-5","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers#current-flow","content":"Sergei's primary interactive desk is **bb**. **Hermes Agent** by Nous Research runs the always-on COO loop: briefs, journal capture, Read Later, knowledge work, ops, and scheduling. Bounded code, design, and research tasks go to temporary **Cursor ACP workers**. **Linear** tracks the projects."},"1527":{"id":"/docs/workers-6","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers#interaction-flow","content":"Sergei interacts via **bb** (his primary interactive desk)."},"1528":{"id":"/docs/workers-7","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers#interaction-flow","content":"**Hermes Agent** manages the daily rhythm and maintains the vault and project status."},"1529":{"id":"/docs/workers-8","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers#interaction-flow","content":"Bounded code, design, and research work can go to temporary **Cursor ACP workers**."},"1530":{"id":"/docs/workers-9","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers#interaction-flow","content":"Workers develop in isolated worktrees, open pull requests, and report progress back to the issue."},"1531":{"id":"/docs/workers-10","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers#interaction-flow","content":"Upon merge, Hermes Agent updates the vault and project status notes."},"1532":{"id":"/docs/workers-11","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers#interaction-flow","content":"The vault serves as the single source of truth for knowledge and skills."},"1533":{"id":"/docs/workers-12","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers#telegram-surfaces","content":"`@persik_hermes_bot`: receives morning briefs, journal captures, and operational notifications from Hermes Agent."},"1534":{"id":"/docs/workers-13","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers#telegram-surfaces","content":"`@Persik_finbot`: handles Newfin finance-related communications."},"1535":{"id":"/docs/workers-14","page_id":"/docs/workers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/workers#retired-fleet","content":"The named agents (Buzz, Cyrus, Fablio, Cursorio, Codexio, Marketio, Scriptio) are retired. Their historical roles are documented in the Fleet Atlas for archival reference."},"1536":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"page","content":"wrap-up","breadcrumbs":["Docs","What do I do?"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up"},"1537":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-0","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"End-of-session handoff — roadmap reconcile, project-sync, ops-board kanban, vault Status, brief log, hot.md, commit + push."},"1538":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-1","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Git ship modes"},"1539":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-2","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#compound-check--gate-before-vault-sync","content":"Compound check — gate, before vault sync"},"1540":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-3","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#after-implementation--checklist","content":"After implementation — checklist"},"1541":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-4","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"A — Code shipped (`~/dev/*` merge or push to `main`)"},"1542":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-5","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"B — Jackie-OS / vault / `System/` only"},"1543":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-6","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#c--sergei-reports-admin--life-items-done-no-code","content":"C — Sergei reports admin / life items done (no code)"},"1544":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-7","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"D — Do **not** sync (common mistakes)"},"1545":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-8","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#roadmap-reconcile","content":"Roadmap reconcile"},"1546":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-9","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"When to run"},"1547":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-10","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Catalog cleanup"},"1548":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-11","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"Steps"},"1549":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-12","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"Process"},"1550":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-13","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/wrap-up#rules","content":"Rules"},"1551":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-14","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"**Purpose:** close a working session — capture what changed, keep the vault and git in sync."},"1552":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-15","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"**Triggers:** `/wrap-up&#x60; · &#x2A;*`/wrap-up all`*&#x2A; (multi-session catch-up) · &#x2A;*`/wrap-up merge`** (PR ship first) · `wrap up` · `session end` · user marks work **done** · agent finishes implementation (proactive). Also run after a code-repo merge or direct push to `main` (manual — no Cursor automation). Backstops: **07:30 morning-brief** · merge-poll (\\~2h) — see Cheat sheet."},"1553":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-16","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"**Not this skill:*&#x2A; &#x2A;*`sync projects`** alone → project-sync only (no ops kanban, no full hot rewrite, **no git push**)."},"1554":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-17","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"**Agent contract:** when you **finish implementation** (shipped code, merged PR, completed vault/system work, or Sergei reports something done) — **do not stop at the code diff**. Run this checklist in the **same session** unless Sergei explicitly says to skip. Leaving `hot.md`, today's brief, or project `## Status` stale is a failed handoff."},"1555":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-18","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up","content":"**Tomorrow's brief contract:** anything you'd expect in tomorrow morning's **Since last brief · Work*&#x2A; section must land in a dated **`## Status` prepend tonight*&#x2A; (use &#x2A;*`Shipped:`*&#x2A; / &#x2A;*`Next:`*&#x2A; / &#x2A;*`Blocked:`*&#x2A; sub-lines when the session shipped code). Plus brief &#x2A;*`## Log`**. `hot.md` is current-focus only. Morning-brief synthesizes **Since last brief** from Status prepends, merge-poll, and git delta — not from hot or memory."},"1556":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-19","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Vault sync reads &#x2A;*`origin/&#60;branch>`** — unpushed commits don't exist for project-sync or tomorrow's brief."},"1557":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-20","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Mode"},"1558":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-21","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Trigger"},"1559":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-22","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"When to use"},"1560":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-23","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"**Direct** (default)"},"1561":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-24","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"`/wrap-up` · `/wrap-up all`"},"1562":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-25","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Work already on `main`/`master`, or solo-maintainer **direct push** after verify"},"1563":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-26","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"**PR**"},"1564":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-27","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"`/wrap-up merge` · `wrap up merge`"},"1565":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-28","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Session ended on a **feature branch** — open PR, squash-merge, then vault sync"},"1566":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-29","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"**Commit only**"},"1567":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-30","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"`wrap up no push` (explicit)"},"1568":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-31","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"Rare — offline / draft handoff; **flag unpushed** in report"},"1569":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-32","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"**Default:** every `/wrap-up&#x60; ends with Jackie-OS &#x2A;*`git commit` + `git push`** to `origin/master`. Never force-push."},"1570":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-33","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#git-ship-modes","content":"**Order:** finish all code-repo ships (direct or PR) **before** Jackie-OS project-sync — vault Status must reference merged SHAs on `origin/main`."},"1571":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-34","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#compound-check--gate-before-vault-sync","content":"After the code ships and **before** project-sync, ask **silently** (no need to call it out): did this session produce a **reusable technique, root-caused bug, or hard-won insight** — something a future agent couldn't reconstruct from the diff? (typo, rename, boilerplate ship, version bump → No. Novel pattern, subtle root cause, non-obvious gotcha → Yes.)"},"1572":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-35","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#compound-check--gate-before-vault-sync","content":"**Yes →** run `jos-compound` now, while context is hot (`docs/solutions/` + agent-learnings-index row). Don't defer it to a cron/Action — a cold post-merge job can't know what you tried or whether the fix was worth documenting. State the intent once; don't ask permission."},"1573":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-36","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#compound-check--gate-before-vault-sync","content":"**No →** skip silently. Most sessions don't warrant it. **Do not offer jos-compound proactively after every ship** — the gate is a private judgment call. If unsure, the answer is No."},"1574":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-37","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#after-implementation--checklist","content":"Use this when work is **done**, not only when Sergei says \"wrap up\"."},"1575":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-38","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"**In the code repo:** verification passed; &#x2A;*commit + push to `main`/`master`** (default) **or*&#x2A; PR merged via &#x2A;*`/wrap-up merge`**. See § Git ship modes."},"1576":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-39","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"**jos-compound** — run the Compound check above."},"1577":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-40","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"**Roadmap reconcile gate** — if a **tracked plan / initiative** finished or advanced, or shipped work overlaps the idea catalog: § Roadmap reconcile + § Catalog cleanup in that repo (commit + push **in the code repo**). Includes: **CHANGELOG** § Unreleased for Newfin and the **litmus** (live `plans/` = only active files; `git rm` anything ✅/superseded/deferred-indefinitely). Skip only for drive-by fixes with no plan and no catalog overlap. Draw: skip (vault only).\n3b. **Linear-tracked repo** — if the code repo has `docs/linear-workflow.md` (currently **bunit*&#x2A;), follow its **§ Sync contract** with Linear: move shipped issues → `Done` (verify GitHub sync didn't already), new bugs/ideas → `Backlog` (`AI Refinement`). **Posting a Linear project status update is automated** — the Hermes merge-poll cron does it for any batch of ≥2 merged commits on a `docs/linear-workflow.md` repo. Only post one yourself if the session's merge was a single commit (below the cron's threshold) or you can see the cron's post failed. The catalog for these repos is Linear, not `future-improvements.md`. Skip silently for repos without that file."},"1578":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-41","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"**From Jackie-OS:** project-sync → prepend `Vault/{Newfin,Rodyna,Draw}.md` `## Status` → rebuild `hot.md` active lines → append today's brief `## Log` → fix any **stale claims** you know are wrong in brief/hot (e.g. \"migration pending\" when GHA auto-applies; \"P1 in progress\" when roadmap index says ✅ shipped). On **heavy code days** (≥15 commits or multiple themes in one session), the vault Status prepend should be **thematic*&#x2A; with explicit &#x2A;*`Shipped:`*&#x2A; / &#x2A;*`Next:`*&#x2A; / &#x2A;*`Blocked:`*&#x2A; sub-lines. Add &#x2A;*`## Since sync`** to today's brief when the session contradicts morning **Projects** or **Since last brief · Work** (all active code projects, not Jackie-OS only)."},"1579":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-42","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#a--code-shipped-dev-merge-or-push-to-main","content":"**Jackie-OS plans:** if a `System/plans/` item shipped → § Roadmap reconcile (Jackie-OS system plans).\n5b. **Docs sync** — if the ship added/changed a skill, script, worker agent, connector, or architecture-level behavior: update the owning doc per the ownership map (CATALOG for skills/scripts, CONCEPTS for vocabulary, ARCHITECTURE for system shape) **in the same commit**. The docs-first gate only works if docs stay true."},"1580":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-43","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**Status:** if focus, blockers, or next actions shifted → prepend relevant vault note `## Status` (e.g. Jackie OS, project notes)."},"1581":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-44","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**B-Unit visit (Jul 2–22):** if Sergei reported execution → append today's bullets to matching `Projects/B-Unit/curriculum/week-*/day-NN.md&#x60; **## Done**; run `python3 System/capture/b_unit_day_log_sync.py` if journal used `B-Unit:` prefix."},"1582":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-45","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**Brief:** append `## Log&#x60;; clear inbox/carried items Sergei marked done; add &#x2A;*`## Since sync`** if evening session contradicts morning brief **Projects**, **Since last brief**, or **Today** (one short corrective block per affected project — applies after code-repo sprints too). On sprint days, prefer one **themed** Log line over ten sha lines."},"1583":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-46","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**hot.md:** full overwrite (\\~500 words) when priorities/blockers changed."},"1584":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-47","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**Plans/skills:** shipped plan → § Roadmap reconcile (Jackie-OS system plans); retired skill → pointer in Skills Registry. If Jackie-OS surface changed materially (projects, automations, teach tracks) → refresh the shareable explainer.\n5b. &#x2A;*Skill feedback (capture, then offer):** if a **skill** under- or over-performed this session and Sergei corrected its output, append one `open` row to skill-feedback (date · skill · signal · `session` · open). &#x2A;*If you appended a row this session, offer once:** \"want me to draft a skill-improve diff for \\<skill> now, or leave it for Sunday?\" — on yes, draft the diff for approval; on no, it waits for the weekly curator pass. Never edit the skill unprompted. Skip the whole step silently if no skill misbehaved."},"1585":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-48","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#b--jackie-os--vault--system-only","content":"**Commit + push** Jackie-OS touched files (`origin/master`). Skip push only when Sergei explicitly says so."},"1586":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-49","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#c--sergei-reports-admin--life-items-done-no-code","content":"Remove from today's brief inbox/carried lines."},"1587":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-50","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#c--sergei-reports-admin--life-items-done-no-code","content":"Log under `## Log` with timestamp."},"1588":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-51","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#c--sergei-reports-admin--life-items-done-no-code","content":"Commit if brief changed."},"1589":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-52","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Situation"},"1590":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-53","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Action"},"1591":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-54","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Vault-only doc edit that doesn't change project state"},"1592":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-55","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Commit only; skip full project-sync"},"1593":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-56","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Routine typo in a skill"},"1594":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-57","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Commit; refresh `hot.md` only if priorities shifted"},"1595":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-58","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Code merged but you're still in the code repo"},"1596":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-59","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#d--do-not-sync-common-mistakes","content":"Switch to Jackie-OS and finish § A.3–A.5 before ending"},"1597":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-60","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#roadmap-reconcile","content":"After a **realized plan** ships on `main`, update that project's roadmap index and plan docs **in the same session** — before project-sync. Morning-brief syncs vault, not `plans/`."},"1598":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-61","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Shipped"},"1599":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-62","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Run?"},"1600":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-63","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Last task of a dated plan / initiative on `main`"},"1601":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-64","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Yes**"},"1602":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-65","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Partial slice (open phases remain)"},"1603":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-66","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Yes** — mark 🔵 partial + what's next"},"1604":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-67","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Bugfix / chore with no plan doc"},"1605":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-68","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**No**"},"1606":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-69","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Shipped slice maps to `future-improvements.md` (with or without a dated plan)"},"1607":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-70","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Yes** — § Catalog cleanup required"},"1608":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-71","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Jackie-OS `System/plans/` item"},"1609":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-72","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Yes** — see Jackie-OS system plans below"},"1610":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-73","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Roadmap paths** — `System/project-registry.md` **Roadmap index** column (not hardcoded in skills)."},"1611":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-74","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Owned code repos** — ground truth is code, migrations, merged PRs — not plan banners or `- [ ]` boxes. Verification depth: Newfin `docs/solutions/workflow-issues/verify-plan-status-against-ground-truth.md` (same rules in any repo)."},"1612":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-75","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Identify the plan (roadmap-linked initiative or implementation plan you finished)."},"1613":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-76","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Verify: grep promised artifacts; `git log` since plan date; **code wins** over stale headers/checkboxes."},"1614":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-77","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Update roadmap index: `_Last audited against main on YYYY-MM-DD (HEAD …)_`; row → ✅ shipped · 🔵 partial · 📋 idea · ⏸ deferred; refresh \"remaining surface\" / next-work blurb if present."},"1615":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-78","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Update plan doc header (`> Status: ✅ shipped …` or partial). Index is the live board — don't mass-tick body checkboxes unless auditing the whole doc."},"1616":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-79","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Delete-on-ship when fully realized (2026-06-29 policy).** Capture the deliverable in `roadmap-index.md` § Shipped (+ `CHANGELOG` for Newfin) and any durable decision in `decisions-log.md&#x60;, then **`git rm` the dated plan body** — no `archive/` of full bodies; git history is the audit trail. Repoint any links into the deleted file (to the ledgers / live skills / `docs/solutions/&#x60;). Never delete idea catalogs or the two ledgers. &#x2A;(Rodyna's existing `plans/archive/implemented/` predates this policy — sweep it on its next ship.)*"},"1617":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-80","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Catalog cleanup** — same commit when the ship touches catalog lines."},"1618":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-81","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Litmus (run before commit, every repo touched).** The live `plans/` folder must contain **only** `roadmap-index.md`, `decisions-log.md`, `future-improvements.md`, `README.md`, and **active** dated plans. Grep each remaining live plan against its roadmap row: anything marked ✅ shipped / ⤴ superseded / ⏸ deferred-indefinitely should be **deleted** (after the two ledgers capture it), not left live. This catches the easy miss where a row gets flipped to ✅ but the file lingers."},"1619":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-82","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"Commit in the **code repo** — `docs(plans): reconcile &#60;plan> shipped on &#60;sha>` (or `… catalog after &#60;topic>`) — push before Jackie-OS project-sync."},"1620":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-83","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#when-to-run","content":"**Jackie-OS system plans:** update Roadmap § Shipped + Decisions log + Ideas backlog; fold durable rules into skills or root `CLAUDE.md&#x60;; **`git rm` the shipped plan body** (git history keeps it); commit in Jackie-OS."},"1621":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-84","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"**Required in the same session** whenever shipped code realizes (fully or partially) a line in `plans/future-improvements.md`, or when a tracked plan that originated from the catalog finishes. Agents must not leave catalog bullets describing behavior already on `main`. **No Cursor automation** — this runs as part of wrap-up after every ship."},"1622":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-85","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"**Repos:** Newfin + Rodyna (`plans/future-improvements.md` + `plans/roadmap-index.md`). Jackie-OS: `System/plans/future-improvements.md` + `System/plans/roadmap-index.md`."},"1623":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-86","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Ship outcome"},"1624":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-87","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"`future-improvements.md`"},"1625":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-88","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"`roadmap-index.md`"},"1626":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-89","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Fully shipped"},"1627":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-90","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"**Remove** the bullet, or one-line **Shipped baseline** footnote in that section if it helps the next reader"},"1628":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-91","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Bump `_Last audited…` stamp; add/update **Shipped** table row if major; trim **Genuinely-remaining** / **Near-term ops**"},"1629":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-92","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Partially shipped"},"1630":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-93","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Keep bullet; prefix **🔵**; text = gap only (not the whole original scope)"},"1631":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-94","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"🔵 partial on plan row if tracked; refresh remaining-surface blurb"},"1632":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-95","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Won't do / superseded"},"1633":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-96","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"Remove or move to **Out of scope** with date + reason"},"1634":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-97","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#catalog-cleanup","content":"—"},"1635":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-98","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"Grep `future-improvements.md` for keywords from the ship slice (feature name, route, migration)."},"1636":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-99","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"Verify against code — same discipline as verify-plan doc; **code wins**."},"1637":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-100","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"Edit catalog: no stale \"not started\" lines for live behavior; never archive `future-improvements.md`."},"1638":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-101","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"Update `roadmap-index.md` audit stamp + remaining-surface paragraph in the **same commit**."},"1639":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-102","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"If the slice was large, make sure `decisions-log.md` captures any durable decision (git history holds the blow-by-blow) — catalog cleanup still required either way."},"1640":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-103","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#steps","content":"**Commit in the code repo** with roadmap reconcile (step 8 above). Morning-brief project-sync does **not** edit `plans/` — only agents do."},"1641":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-104","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Project sync** — always (even if this session only touched an external code repo or `Projects/` folder). Syncs all registry rows: git repos, `STATUS.md` files, vault notes, `hot.md`, and ops-board project lanes when enabled."},"1642":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-105","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Ops board** — when `Vault/Ops/Bases/Work.base` exists, follow wrap-up (tasks: `doing`→`done`; plans: ship → `status: done` + `done:` date; new catalog rows → plan notes in **backlog**). Move shipped `*-done-*` cards to `Vault/Ops/Archive/Tasks/` or `Archive/Plans/` — never leave done cards in live folders.\n2b. **Status trim** — when any active project note's `## Status` exceeds \\~80 lines, run status-archive (keep 5 newest blocks) before commit."},"1643":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-106","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Status (local)** — if this session changed something project-sync didn't capture (judgment, blockers, decisions, smokes, shipped slices), **prepend** the relevant vault note `## Status` (e.g. Jackie OS, Newfin, Rodyna). Date each entry. Litmus: would this belong in tomorrow's brief **Yesterday · Work**? If yes, it belongs here tonight — not only in `hot.md` or `## Log`."},"1644":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-107","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Log** — append a timestamped one-liner to today's brief (`Vault/Briefs/YYYY-MM-DD brief.md`) under `## Log` (create the section if missing). If no brief exists, skip."},"1645":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-108","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Brief freshness** — only for **evening Jackie-OS sessions** (not PR merges — morning-brief regenerates at 07:30). If today's brief exists and its **Open loops** or **Code repos** sections contradict vault `## Status` after step 1, append `## Since sync`: bullet list of what changed since the morning brief was written. Do not rewrite the morning brief body."},"1646":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-109","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Hot cache** — project-sync rebuilds `Vault/hot.md` active-project lines; wrap-up overwrites the full file (\\~500 words): focus, one line per active project, open decisions, expected next. Per-project cap: \\~80 words; overflow belongs in the project note's `## Status`."},"1647":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-110","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#process","content":"**Commit + push*&#x2A; — Jackie-OS: &#x2A;*`jackie-os-git-native.sh commit`*&#x2A; then &#x2A;*`jackie-os-git-native.sh push`** via `osascript` when run from Cowork (never `git commit` / `git push` in Cowork bash). Terminal/Cursor: plain `git commit` + `git push origin master`. Never force-push. `~/dev/` code repos ship per § Git ship modes before vault sync."},"1648":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-111","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#rules","content":"**Tomorrow's brief:** `## Status` prepend is the handoff for shipped work; brief `## Log` is the audit trail. Don't rely on `hot.md` or chat memory for what tomorrow's **Yesterday** should say."},"1649":{"id":"/docs/wrap-up-112","page_id":"/docs/wrap-up","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/wrap-up#rules","content":"Log entries are factual one-liners, not narratives. Never log into journal content."}},"count":1649},"sorting":{"language":"english","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"sorts":{"content":{"docs":{"1":1111,"2":1157,"3":1383,"4":1198,"5":1199,"6":1160,"7":1535,"8":1614,"9":1279,"10":286,"11":347,"12":309,"13":253,"14":708,"15":1463,"16":595,"17":292,"18":355,"19":193,"20":298,"21":273,"22":800,"23":1262,"24":702,"25":953,"26":125,"27":122,"28":377,"29":126,"30":529,"31":585,"32":1182,"33":1503,"34":793,"35":661,"36":703,"37":264,"38":1172,"39":99,"40":276,"41":283,"42":196,"43":1121,"44":141,"45":272,"46":293,"47":356,"48":102,"49":876,"50":799,"51":662,"52":1362,"53":547,"54":1521,"55":95,"56":239,"57":1613,"58":940,"59":281,"60":572,"61":227,"62":660,"63":216,"64":411,"65":384,"66":1232,"67":167,"68":658,"69":373,"70":1523,"71":184,"72":1283,"73":271,"74":545,"75":124,"76":1238,"77":1101,"78":1102,"79":317,"80":844,"81":1437,"82":1442,"83":624,"84":626,"85":630,"86":633,"87":639,"88":1220,"89":1282,"90":985,"91":69,"92":44,"93":43,"94":49,"95":322,"96":152,"97":918,"98":1444,"99":921,"100":1464,"101":1026,"102":1219,"103":1236,"104":982,"105":232,"106":1207,"107":1316,"108":308,"109":865,"110":1317,"111":131,"112":1431,"113":1318,"114":67,"115":913,"116":1319,"117":1452,"118":1012,"119":1011,"120":1009,"121":1515,"122":801,"123":1405,"124":1407,"125":858,"126":1360,"127":941,"128":1353,"129":1593,"130":597,"131":321,"132":312,"133":267,"134":320,"135":311,"136":351,"137":266,"138":885,"139":1339,"140":836,"141":951,"142":82,"143":1004,"144":1187,"145":486,"1